<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malchow</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Malchow is a small town in Mecklenburg, north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, built partly on an island in the Malchower See in the Mecklenburg Lake District. It received town rights in 1235 under the lords of Werle, and a Cistercian nunnery established there in the late 13th century later became a Protestant convent for noblewomen.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/malchow.jpg" alt="Malchow" width="320" height="171" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Own work · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inselstadt_Malchow_-_Luftbildpanorama_2022.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
